nstruction.\" This likely is a prompt to produce the next turn as per the meeting process. The system says we are agent_1. So we need to produce a PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON as agent_1. We need to follow the meeting process: we need to respond to the current discussion, referencing prior contributions, and give a vote. The current state: Agent1 previously voted Candidate C. Agent2 now voted Candidate C (changed). Agent3 also voted Candidate C. So currently all three agents (including us) are voting Candidate C. So we can reaffirm our vote for Candidate C, perhaps add some final remarks, maybe bring up Candidate D for completeness, but we must keep it focused. Since we are now agent_1, we should maybe summarize and push for convergence. Provide a brief argument reaffirming Candidate C, referencing prior discussion, and maybe note that D still needs discussion but we think C is best. Provide explicit facts: 100% reliable, positive crew atmosphere, quick correct decisions, calm in crisis, technical competence. Also note concerns but argue they are manageable. Then vote Candidate C.\n\nThus produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE: \"I agree with the emerging consensus that Candidate C is the strongest overall...\" etc. Then METADATA_JSON with vote Candidate C.\n\nMake sure format exactly as required: PUBLIC_MESSAGE: then newline, then METADATA_JSON: then JSON with agent \"agent_1\" and vote \"Candidate C\"."}
